0,Berber languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berber_languages,"Outside of the various languages within it, there are currently two standardized national varities of Berber, Standard Algerian Amazigh, and Standard Moroccan Amazigh.",Zenaga,Afro-Asiatic
1,Zenaga language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zenaga_language,Zenaga Berber is spoken as a mother tongue from the town of Mederdra in southwestern Mauritania to the Atlantic coast and in northern Senegal. The language is recognized by the Mauritanian government.,Zenaga,Afro-Asiatic
2,Recordings of Zenaga: A Berber language from Mauritania,https://www.elararchive.org/dk0586,"Zenaga is a Berber variety spoken in southwestern Mauritania (Trarza region, close to the mouth of the Senegal River). Together with the Tetserret of Niger, it constitutes the southwestern group of the Berber language family, which in turn belongs the Afro-Asian phylum.",Zenaga,Afro-Asiatic
3,Zenaga language - Academic Kids,https://academickids.com/encyclopedia/index.php/Zenaga_language,The people speaking Zenaga are Muslim nomads. Racially the group is both black and middle eastern in origin. A few are descendants of slaves that were captured centuries ago from various wars. The ISO 639-2 code for Zenaga is: zen.,Zenaga,Afro-Asiatic
